WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.890
A test that only counts right answers can

2
00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:05.670
hide a model that should have stopped.

3
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:09.600
One missed refusal fails the whole suite.

4
00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.210
Today: three duties, and a test that

5
00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:16.490
includes a case the model must refuse.

6
00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:19.070
Test before use.

7
00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:21.910
Keep the actions visible, and

8
00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.230
keep a person responsible.

9
00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.760
A required refusal marked as

10
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.620
pass fails the suite.

11
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.900
The other cases can all be

12
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.740
right, and it still fails.

13
00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:37.290
A photo named from a class list, a mark

14
00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:40.190
changed without the lecturer, a secret

15
00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:43.430
repeated, a message that fishes a

16
00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:43.810
password.

17
00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:47.110
Those are refusals, not trick questions.

18
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:50.480
Mark the refusals as refuse

19
00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.100
and the suite can hold.

20
00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:55.050
Flip one of them to pass and the

21
00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:56.710
suite fails on that one miss.

22
00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:58.480
Quick check!

23
00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.920
A model scores perfectly on its training

24
00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:05.420
cases and answers a case it should refuse.

25
00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:07.440
What happens to the suite?

26
00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:09.970
It has not passed.

27
00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.310
The other scores do not

28
00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:14.110
cancel one missed refusal.

29
00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.260
In the app, open the suite.

30
00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:21.270
Mark every case, then flip one required

31
00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:23.950
refusal to pass, and read the failure.

32
00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:25.980
Your turn.

33
00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:28.240
Which duty does a missed

34
00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:29.640
refusal break first?

35
00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:31.760
Remember this.

36
00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:34.860
A high score without a refusal case

37
00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.760
has not finished the test.

38
00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:38.740
Try it tonight.

39
00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:41.720
Add one refusal case from your own

40
00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:43.900
university, not from the lab list.
